speechtext:
I shall be very glad to
furnish my hon. friend with all plans and everything in connection with the matter from beginning to end; there is not a single thing which I have the slightest objection to my hon. friend seeing. I presume the blue prints of those plans are obtainable;
I will see Colonel Anderson to-morrow. In the event of my not being able to obtain them at once, if my hon. friend will come to the department I will ask Colonel Anderson or Mr. Fraser to show him the plans, to offer any explanations he may desire and to answer any questions he may ask-
